course: dictionary
lesson: 6717
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word «office» can mean a room where people work, a place where a service is given, or an important job. The sentence around it tells you which meaning the writer chose.
explain: «If nobody comes to pick you up, go back into the school office and tell a teacher.» Here an office is a room in the school where people work and visitors go. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: «You can still check: what does the official election office say?» Here an office is a building where a service is given, so the meaning is different. Context is the clue that tells you which meaning to use.
fact: An office is a room or building where people work at desks.
fact: An office can also be a place where a service is given, such as a post office, a ticket office or a box office.
fact: An office can be an important job or position, as in «the office of president».
fact: Phrases with office: head teacher's office, office worker, in office.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word the writer means.
exercise: «If nobody comes to pick you up, go back into the school office and tell a teacher.» What kind of place is the school office? | *A room in the school where people work | A desk you write at | An important job, like president | A kind of lift
exercise: «You can still check: what does the official election office say?» What does office mean here? | *A building where a service is given | A cupboard for coats | A room with a computer and a printer | A job in government
exercise: Ella reads «the office of president» and says office is a room. What does office mean here? | A kind of desk | A room where people sit at desks | A place where tickets are sold | *An important job or position
test: Which phrase means a place where tickets are sold? | *Box office | Office worker | Head teacher's office | In office
test: In «the school office», what is the best way to check the meaning of office? | *Read the words around it and try each meaning in the sentence | Skip the word and never come back to it | Guess the first meaning you think of and never check | Look only at the word's first letter
exam: Pupil asks: office has four meanings, so how do I pick the right one? | Always choose the room meaning | *Read the sentence around it, try each meaning, and choose the one that makes sense | Always choose the job meaning | Pick the longest meaning
